* The FRI toolbox\ntwelve cards
** Codes and radii
*** Reed-Solomon code\n//polynomial → evaluations; different polynomials rarely agree//
*** Rate\n//rho = d/n; every bound is a function of it//
*** Delta-far\n//far = wrong in more than a delta fraction//
*** Unique decoding distance\n//below (1-rho)/2, exactly one candidate//
*** Johnson bound\n//1 - sqrt(rho); few candidates; the proofs stop here//
** Oracle proofs
*** Interactive oracle proof (IOP)\n//strings sent, dice rolled, a few cells read//
*** IOP of proximity (IOPP)\n//accept codewords, reject the far, promise nothing between//
*** BCS compiler\n//Merkle roots + Fiat-Shamir turn an IOP into a SNARK//
left side
** Evaluation proofs
*** Quotienting\n//(u - b)/(x - a): evaluation claim → proximity claim//
*** DEEP\n//one random (r, s) outside the domain pins one polynomial//
** Distance-preserving maps
*** Proximity gap theorem\n//a far word cannot hide in a random blend//
*** Folding\n//even + r · odd; half the degree, distance kept//
@endmindmap
